    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Christian kingdom of the Middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-dongola">Old Dongola</a>, that absorbed neighbouring Nobadia by about 700.</li><li>Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a> repelled Arab invasions in 642 and 652, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baqt">Baqt treaty</a> kept it independent for some six centuries.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> intervention from 1276, Arab migration and civil war broke the kingdom, and the court left Dongola in the 1360s.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Arab writers called the Makurian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a> the pupil-smiters, because they aimed at their enemies' eyes and blinded many of the invaders in 642 and 652.</p></aside>
    </section>

